From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Lazarev <lazarev@tactiqedge.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm: dts: bcm2711-rpi-4-b: pin mmc0 to the SD card in
 U-Boot's own tree

With OF_BOARD off (see 0001), U-Boot uses its own control devicetree
instead of the one the VideoCore firmware passes. The firmware's tree
has mmc aliases that make the SD card mmc 0; U-Boot's tree has none, so
device numbers follow bind order, and the Wi-Fi SDIO controller under
/soc is bound before the SD controller under /emmc2bus.

Add bcm2711-rpi-4-b-u-boot.dtsi with mmc0 = &emmc2 and mmc1 = &sdhci.
A board-specific -u-boot.dtsi replaces the automatic inclusion of
bcm283x-u-boot.dtsi, so the new file includes it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [TactiQ trust model: only needed with OF_BOARD off]
---
 arch/arm/dts/bcm2711-rpi-4-b-u-boot.dtsi | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/dts/bcm2711-rpi-4-b-u-boot.dtsi

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/bcm2711-rpi-4-b-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/bcm2711-rpi-4-b-u-boot.dtsi
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2312a88
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/bcm2711-rpi-4-b-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+
+/*
+ * U-Boot additions for the Raspberry Pi 4 Model B devicetree when U-Boot
+ * uses its own control devicetree (OF_BOARD off).
+ *
+ * Its presence replaces the automatic inclusion of bcm283x-u-boot.dtsi
+ * (scripts/Makefile.lib takes the first match), so that file is included
+ * here explicitly.
+ */
+
+#include "bcm283x-u-boot.dtsi"
+
+/*
+ * The firmware's devicetree pins mmc0 to the SD card; this tree has no mmc
+ * aliases, so device numbers would follow bind order, in which the Wi-Fi
+ * SDIO controller under /soc comes before the SD controller. Pin them, so
+ * that "mmc 0" in the environment is the SD card.
+ */
+/ {
+	aliases {
+		mmc0 = &emmc2;
+		mmc1 = &sdhci;
+	};
+};
